                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "35a6d811-36f8-34b4-9dcd-d9425e5bbb57",
                        "entry_id": "9e568ede-bbf0-3b6c-bad9-d5a2067058fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "неодуш., прост. жадность"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "87c140b5-7d32-4f23-8427-20514c22c244",
                                "sense_id": "35a6d811-36f8-34b4-9dcd-d9425e5bbb57",
                                "text": "Дело пошло с того, что Лазарь, с немалою скорбию, посетовал на засуху, но и посетовал лишь потому, что она, засуха эта, лишала его крупных барышей, ибо по её милости вода спала и мельница почти перестала работать. Мельничиха и договорить ему не дала. ― Ох, не скупись, ох, не поддавайся жадобе, Лазарь, ― горячо и настойчиво заговорила она, ― али не упомнишь, откуда произошли?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5249f9a8-326a-42cc-8cd2-7838dab6c328",
                                "sense_id": "35a6d811-36f8-34b4-9dcd-d9425e5bbb57",
                                "text": "И все они не раз кляли Демьяна, дравшего с них за помол по восьми фунтов с пуда, да ещё и старавшегося обсчитать, обвесить, за жадобу ненасытную."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "66f2772d-0d09-4e21-9a2d-6202a7b582be",
                                "sense_id": "35a6d811-36f8-34b4-9dcd-d9425e5bbb57",
                                "text": "И вовсе не из чёрствости, ревности или самолюбивой жадобы, а просто всё её существо было полно им, ни для кого иного не открывалось места."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6fe9e2e2-7b37-316c-892c-ae9316014e0b",
                        "entry_id": "9e568ede-bbf0-3b6c-bad9-d5a2067058fe",
                        "glosses": [
                            "перен., прост. жадный и скупой человек"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "5e48a5c4-4897-40f5-b427-41b9597cbbbe",
                                "sense_id": "6fe9e2e2-7b37-316c-892c-ae9316014e0b",
                                "text": "..Всыпь на цигарочку, Прошка! А и жадоба ж ты! Забыл, как я тебе под Белавином красноармейские ботинки отдал?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "06b10394-2c37-413d-bfac-72e22415199c",
                                "sense_id": "6fe9e2e2-7b37-316c-892c-ae9316014e0b",
                                "text": "Ко мне пол-Грузии за дурью ездит ― и все жадобы, лишь бы урвать побольше, а там пусть всё огнём горит!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7db220e1-1985-4f48-980d-b0423c520f08",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e568ede-bbf0-3b6c-bad9-d5a2067058fe",
                        "source_sense_description": "жадность",
                        "target_lang_word": "greed",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "greed",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "8bff3a12-6956-38c5-9db7-39123cafa205",
                                        "entry_id": "55171cf4-41ee-31f1-9eaa-90671c1faec9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A selfish or excessive desire for more than is needed or deserved, especially of money, wealth, food, or other possessions."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9830e570-5c1d-4e67-a317-8fd1cee96526",
                                                "sense_id": "8bff3a12-6956-38c5-9db7-39123cafa205",
                                                "text": "His greed was his undoing."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9998a4c5-5551-4fed-990c-e7cd09736564",
                                                "sense_id": "8bff3a12-6956-38c5-9db7-39123cafa205",
                                                "text": "[…]But when I had bestridden the plank, quoth I to myself, \"Thou deserveth all that betideth thee. All this is decreed to me of Allah (whose name be exalted!), to turn me from my greed of gain, whence ariseth all that I endure, for I have wealth galore.\""
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "090ab8ff-1782-428a-8903-372d23ae4873",
                                                "sense_id": "8bff3a12-6956-38c5-9db7-39123cafa205",
                                                "text": "Your market gardener is not a well-breeched man, dependant as he is on the imponderables of glut, the inequities of distribution, and the greeds of wholesaler and retailer."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "da05c7f1-cd52-47e9-95d3-7e40241c412f",
                                                "sense_id": "8bff3a12-6956-38c5-9db7-39123cafa205",
                                                "text": "She does not display voracities and greeds like a number of patients […] nor has she shown any significant tendency to possessiveness, grievance, paranoia, or mania."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e472d04f-fceb-4cd9-8cc5-a17da0d738e1",
                                                "sense_id": "8bff3a12-6956-38c5-9db7-39123cafa205",
                                                "text": "The point is, ladies and gentleman, that greed, for lack of a better word, is good. Greed is right, greed works. Greed clarifies, cuts through, and captures the essence of the evolutionary spirit. Greed, in all of its forms; greed for life, for money, for love, knowledge has marked the upward surge of mankind."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "greed",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ec41933d-5820-3913-b821-23406d83c31e",
                                        "entry_id": "0cc97faf-bca1-385b-82df-ecd5dd0fbb81",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To desire in a greedy manner, or to act on such a desire."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f8670af7-9cad-404b-8633-d597266d1af5",
                                                "sense_id": "ec41933d-5820-3913-b821-23406d83c31e",
                                                "text": "The ravens sit greeding, / And watching, and heeding: / Thoro' wind, over water, / Comes scent of the slaughter, / And ravens sit greeding / Their share of the bones."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0808650-caae-47d5-bdb8-af9168706414",
                                                "sense_id": "ec41933d-5820-3913-b821-23406d83c31e",
                                                "text": "Hearing these words he arose, because indeed he greeded for her, and came up behind her as she rested upon her elbows and knees and bending in hand his prickle nailed it into her coynte and did manly devoir."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de2fb649-fa3f-42e7-8e14-1be5d6d1a96a",
                                                "sense_id": "ec41933d-5820-3913-b821-23406d83c31e",
                                                "text": "This conniving bastard has greeded the farm off an old man and I end up with nothing."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "b730b05e-b8df-4cdc-ad6e-13a26e2799a2",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e568ede-bbf0-3b6c-bad9-d5a2067058fe",
                        "source_sense_description": "жадность",
                        "target_lang_word": "greediness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "greediness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "95d7859f-422f-39b9-81c7-8487d3aa8e71",
                                        "entry_id": "e66ff6fc-5f5e-3ece-a466-bb673954707c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The state of being greedy; greed."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "88501a69-e290-4be2-9061-faf0a003c8b4",
                                                "sense_id": "95d7859f-422f-39b9-81c7-8487d3aa8e71",
                                                "text": "Thereto the body of a dog she had, / Full of fell ravin and fierce greedinesse […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "fd964ffa-5f05-4a36-a302-3b947e092f56",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e568ede-bbf0-3b6c-bad9-d5a2067058fe",
                        "source_sense_description": "жадность",
                        "target_lang_word": "avarice",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "avarice",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4d52c8ff-4142-31ec-b87e-8e840e62f5d3",
                                        "entry_id": "e56b3904-fb76-377f-be1f-29fed1084b85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Excessive or inordinate desire of gain; greed for wealth"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ee0eeda6-4b62-483f-92d7-de6543eed565",
                                                "sense_id": "4d52c8ff-4142-31ec-b87e-8e840e62f5d3",
                                                "text": "By multiplying the means of gratification, by promoting the introduction and circulation of the precious metals, those darling objects of human avarice and enterprise, it serves to vivify and invigorate the channels of industry, and to make them flow with greater activity and copiousness."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "fa6a8dda-d502-3a34-ad9b-a26aa89bda33",
                                        "entry_id": "e56b3904-fb76-377f-be1f-29fed1084b85",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Inordinate desire for some supposed good."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d3414249-6d8b-47c0-86a0-09438eb1e407",
                        "source_entry_id": "9e568ede-bbf0-3b6c-bad9-d5a2067058fe",
                        "source_sense_description": "жадность",
                        "target_lang_word": "covetousness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "covetousness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                        "entry_id": "ff4c7187-3bb1-3bf6-8373-7822b1020ec2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Immoderate desire for the possession of something, especially for wealth."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable",
                                            "usually"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "27d168b1-3967-43b9-a166-f6c8f2f2fae3",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                                "text": "He which will yield to Fear. muſt neceſſarily yield to Covetouſneſs or any inordinate Deſire."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ade1bdf3-53b3-4b46-bce0-b0930ca9f633",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                                "text": "Covetouſneſs is the yelow Jaundice of the foul, which ariſes from the over-flowing of the heart with love to yellow gold, by which a Chriſtian is dull'd and deadned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b52549ec-f66b-4575-90fd-75aa966b4191",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                                "text": "Covetousness prevents all good, and is and inlet and encouragement to evil."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b510ebdb-7f96-458a-b139-5f5fd85a27b4",
                                                "sense_id": "3ad39934-2e34-37b7-9c62-6ac9dc1a3cf0",
                                                "text": "In obvious compensation and opposition the fear of nothingness becomes the source of covetousness..."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7e9427aa-dadd-49d2-88e9-ec0b840c2cbe",
